  "caption": "Figure B.1: Schematic for training across extreme light levels. Step 1: PR-CNN model was trained end-to-end to predict Rat Retina ’A’ RGC responses at photopic light level (10,000 R*rod−1s−1). This led to an estimate for cone photoreceptor parameters and a model for the inner retina circuit (the CNN layers). Step 2: The model was re-trained at scotopic light level (1 R*rod−1s−1) but the CNN layers were set to non-trainable and fixed to weights learnt in Step 1. In this case, the photoreceptor model learnt parameters reflecting rods. Step 3: The model was trained to predict Rat Retina ’B’ responses at photopic light level. Photoreceptor layer was set to non-trainable with parameters fixed to cone parameters learnt in Step 1. Step 4 (testing step): Model was tested to predict Rat Retina ’B’ responses at scotopic light level. Here, we used the rod photoreceptor parameters learnt in Step 2 and rest of the model representing inner retina pathways of Retina B learnt in Step 3.",
